/-! # A relative power-series diagram with prescribed coefficients

Source: Stacks Project, More on Algebra, Tag 07NQ, proof of (2) implies (3),
and Algebra, Tag 0C0S (2), coefficient-preserving diagram refinement
(blueprint: lem-trf-relative-power-series-fibre-diagram).

The two variable blocks are indexed by `Fin e ⊕ Fin s`. The canonical map `j` is
`rename Sum.inl` after coefficient extension by `ResidueField.map f`; the map `p`
is `killCompl Function.Embedding.inr`. Continuity is expressed by ideal powers,
without choosing topological-space instances. For the equivalence `ρ`, the comap
identity expresses continuity in both directions and preservation of maximal ideals.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v

namespace IsLocalRing

/-- A regular complete closed fibre gives a coefficient-preserving surjective relative
power-series evaluation, with kernel in the ideal of base variables.
Source: Stacks Project, Tags 07NQ (special-fibre diagram) and 0C0S (2)
(blueprint: lem-trf-relative-power-series-fibre-diagram).

Proof, following the node's six steps:
1. Since f is local, mB is contained in n, and C = B/mB has residue field L.
Choose s generators of its maximal ideal by regularity and dimension, and lift
these to t_i in n. The coefficient map πb induces the identity on L. Apply
lem-trf-regular-complete-coefficient-coordinates to these generators and πb to obtain ρ.
2. Apply lem-weil-pbc-power-series-field-cohen-regular-complete to K and L to give
R and S their complete Noetherian local structures and variable-generated maximal ideals.
Coefficient extension followed by rename Sum.inl defines j. It sends the maximal ideal
into the maximal ideal and is local. The deletion map p is surjective with kernel (X)S
by lem-weil-pbc-power-series-quotient-variables, after reindexing the two finite blocks.
3. Apply lem-weil-pbc-power-series-adic-evaluation to b and the list f(x_i), t_i in n.
Completeness of B gives v, continuous with the stated values. It is local since all
variables map into n and its constants reduce to the identity of L.
4. The evaluated variables generate n: modulo mB the t_i generate, and mB itself is
generated by the f(x_i). Constants surject onto L. Apply
lem-weil-pbc-complete-source-surjective-mod-ideal to the complete source S and the
n-adically Hausdorff target B to conclude v is surjective.
5. The continuous maps vj and fq agree on K by coefficient compatibility, and on X_i
by construction. Evaluation uniqueness gives vj = fq. Similarly πv and ρp agree on L,
on every X_i (both zero), and on T_i. Evaluation uniqueness gives πv = ρp.
6. For F in ker v, the second identity gives ρ(p(F)) = 0. Injectivity of ρ implies
p(F) = 0, so F belongs to ker p = (X)S. Empty lists cause no exception: if s = 0,
ρ is the coefficient isomorphism; if e = 0, p is the identity under the canonical
reindexing and v is injective; if both vanish, v is the coefficient isomorphism.
-/
theorem exists_relative_power_series_fibre_diagram
    (A : Type u) (B : Type v) [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [IsLocalRing A] [IsLocalRing B]
    [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsNoetherianRing B]
    (f : A →+* B) [IsLocalHom f]
    [IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal A) A] [IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal B) B]
    (a : ResidueField A →+* A) (b : ResidueField B →+* B)
    (ha : (residue A).comp a = RingHom.id (ResidueField A))
    (hb : (residue B).comp b = RingHom.id (ResidueField B))
    (hab : b.comp (ResidueField.map f) = f.comp a)
    (e : ℕ) (x : Fin e → A)
    (hx : Ideal.span (Set.range x) = maximalIdeal A)
    (q : MvPowerSeries (Fin e) (ResidueField A) →+* A) [IsLocalHom q]
    (hq : Function.Surjective q)
    (hqC : ∀ k : ResidueField A, q (MvPowerSeries.C k) = a k)
    (hqX : ∀ i : Fin e, q (MvPowerSeries.X i) = x i)
    (hqcont : ∀ N : ℕ, ∃ M : ℕ,
      ∀ F ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range
        (MvPowerSeries.X : Fin e → MvPowerSeries (Fin e) (ResidueField A))) ^ M,
        q F ∈ maximalIdeal A ^ N)
    [IsRegularLocalRing (B ⧸ (maximalIdeal A).map f)]
    [IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal (B ⧸ (maximalIdeal A).map f))
      (B ⧸ (maximalIdeal A).map f)]
    (s : ℕ) (hdim : ringKrullDim (B ⧸ (maximalIdeal A).map f) = (s : WithBot ℕ∞)) :
    IsNoetherianRing (MvPowerSeries (Fin e ⊕ Fin s) (ResidueField B)) ∧
    IsLocalRing (MvPowerSeries (Fin e ⊕ Fin s) (ResidueField B)) ∧
    IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin e ⊕ Fin s) (ResidueField B)))
      (MvPowerSeries (Fin e ⊕ Fin s) (ResidueField B)) ∧
    maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin e ⊕ Fin s) (ResidueField B)) =
      Ideal.span (Set.range (MvPowerSeries.X :
        Fin e ⊕ Fin s → MvPowerSeries (Fin e ⊕ Fin s) (ResidueField B))) ∧
    IsLocalHom ((MvPowerSeries.rename (Sum.inl : Fin e → Fin e ⊕ Fin s)).toRingHom.comp
      (MvPowerSeries.map (ResidueField.map f))) ∧
    Function.Surjective (MvPowerSeries.killCompl (R := ResidueField B)
      (Function.Embedding.inr : Fin s ↪ Fin e ⊕ Fin s)) ∧
    RingHom.ker (MvPowerSeries.killCompl (R := ResidueField B)
      (Function.Embedding.inr : Fin s ↪ Fin e ⊕ Fin s)).toRingHom =
      Ideal.span (Set.range (fun i : Fin e ↦
        (MvPowerSeries.X (Sum.inl i) : MvPowerSeries (Fin e ⊕ Fin s) (ResidueField B)))) ∧
    ∃ (t : Fin s → B)
      (ρ : MvPowerSeries (Fin s) (ResidueField B) ≃+* (B ⧸ (maximalIdeal A).map f)),
      (∀ i : Fin s, t i ∈ maximalIdeal B) ∧
      Ideal.span (Set.range (fun i : Fin s ↦
        Ideal.Quotient.mk ((maximalIdeal A).map f) (t i))) =
        maximalIdeal (B ⧸ (maximalIdeal A).map f) ∧
      (∀ l : ResidueField B,
        ρ (MvPowerSeries.C l) = Ideal.Quotient.mk ((maximalIdeal A).map f) (b l)) ∧
      (∀ i : Fin s,
        ρ (MvPowerSeries.X i) = Ideal.Quotient.mk ((maximalIdeal A).map f) (t i)) ∧
      (∀ N : ℕ, Ideal.comap ρ.toRingHom
        (maximalIdeal (B ⧸ (maximalIdeal A).map f) ^ N) =
        Ideal.span (Set.range
          (MvPowerSeries.X : Fin s → MvPowerSeries (Fin s) (ResidueField B))) ^ N) ∧
      ∃ v : MvPowerSeries (Fin e ⊕ Fin s) (ResidueField B) →+* B,
        Function.Surjective v ∧ IsLocalHom v ∧
        (∀ N : ℕ, ∃ M : ℕ,
          ∀ F ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range (MvPowerSeries.X :
            Fin e ⊕ Fin s → MvPowerSeries (Fin e ⊕ Fin s) (ResidueField B))) ^ M,
            v F ∈ maximalIdeal B ^ N) ∧
        (∀ l : ResidueField B, v (MvPowerSeries.C l) = b l) ∧
        (∀ i : Fin e, v (MvPowerSeries.X (Sum.inl i)) = f (x i)) ∧
        (∀ i : Fin s, v (MvPowerSeries.X (Sum.inr i)) = t i) ∧
        v.comp ((MvPowerSeries.rename (Sum.inl : Fin e → Fin e ⊕ Fin s)).toRingHom.comp
          (MvPowerSeries.map (ResidueField.map f))) = f.comp q ∧
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk ((maximalIdeal A).map f)).comp v =
          ρ.toRingHom.comp (MvPowerSeries.killCompl (R := ResidueField B)
            (Function.Embedding.inr : Fin s ↪ Fin e ⊕ Fin s)).toRingHom ∧
        RingHom.ker v ≤ Ideal.span (Set.range (fun i : Fin e ↦
          (MvPowerSeries.X (Sum.inl i) :
            MvPowerSeries (Fin e ⊕ Fin s) (ResidueField B)))) := by
  sorry

end IsLocalRing
